# Predictive Maintenance Lab — Core

Local GRU/LSTM prototype: bearings RUL (XJTU-SY) and filter time-to-600 Pa (HSE, censored). Package lives in `src/pdm/`. UI English. Spec: `Cursor_Predictive_Maintenance_MVP_Spec.md`.

**Stack:** Python ≥3.11 (tested 3.12) · PyTorch · Streamlit · Plotly · numpy/pandas/scipy · scikit-learn · pyarrow · PyYAML · pytest · ruff

**Out of MVP:** FastAPI/React, Docker, MLflow, TensorFlow, Transformers, OpenAI SDK, extra NN architectures, live SCADA.

**Layout:**
- `src/pdm/` — CLI, train/eval, Streamlit `app.py`, worker, models, replay
- `src/pdm/data/` — XJTU-SY + HSE loaders, download, prepare
- `configs/{bearings,filters}.yaml` — dataset defaults
- `tests/` — spec invariants + Streamlit AppTest
- `data/`, `runs/`, `.venv/` — never commit

**Principles:**
- Always `.venv` Python: `.venv/bin/python -m pdm …`
- No leakage: train-only scalers; whole-unit splits; predictor never sees future rows or reference RUL
- Architectures: **GRU or LSTM only**; separate weights/scalers per dataset; never load a bearings checkpoint into filters
- Heavy jobs in `pdm.worker` (one at a time); UI binds `127.0.0.1:8501`
- Real data only. Do not invent MAT/CSV fields. `filters_full_history` is disabled (MATLAB table unreadable)

**Verify before claiming done:**
```bash
.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests -q
.venv/bin/python -m ruff check src tests
```
UI changes: Streamlit `AppTest` in `tests/test_worker_and_app.py` or exercise `http://127.0.0.1:8501`. `--smoke` runs are not quality claims.
